  {
    "episode_id": 89378,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89378.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'm not going to give it all away here on your... Understood. But I will say that because of the five-minute questioning, what I'm trying to advise all of our members to not do is don't give a three-minute speech and then ask a wide-ranging question that then just allows Mueller to pontificate and say nothing. So what I'm going to try to do, what our team is going to do, the Republicans, at least on the House Intelligence Committee. So we're going to try to work through a bunch of questions that need to be answered. You know, yes or no questions. And there's some real simple ones out there, like to start with, did you know that Andrew Weisman was and was briefed on the dossier in the summer of 2016. And that's an easy one to start",
