    "turn_text": "Yeah? So the way what I understand and this is just from press reports that those are those DOJ officials are actually Horowitz, the inspector general's investigators. So supposedly they set down with him for what seems like a fairly lengthy amount of time, able to ask him some questions. Now, this will be another thing that will be a whole nother podcast, but the media is culpable on this. So you had a great example of four major media outlets cover that these inspector general, the Horowitz people, interviewed Christopher Steele. Now, all four of these outlets are all what I call Russia hoaxers. So they're media people that are well into the Russia hoax. They wrote, you know, numerous Russia hoax stories. Now I can tell you, you know, with almost 100% certainty, the investigators did not brief. The DOJ investigators, Horvitz investigators, did not brief these four Russia hoax reporters. The only people that it could have been is somebody who talked to Christopher Steele. What's a common theme through all four of these media reports? It's all a common theme. What a great person Christopher Steele was and how cooperative he was. This is just an absolute joke. At some point, the media has got to be held accountable, especially the ones that are official Russia hoaxers. There's probably a good three to four dozen major media folks that are Russia hoaxers. And, you know, it's an embarrassment to the profession. But worse than that, it's degraded the ability of the press. And, you know, we all have our first amendment rights. We have the press has their rights to investigate things. But, you know, not when they're essentially being partisan assets, you know, assets for Christopher Steele, Fusion GPS. You know, we know that Fusion GPS and Christopher Steele were briefing reporters. And the fact that reporters will be so lazy, so disingenuous, so dishonest to take any information from Fusion GPS or Christopher Steele at this point. You know, they probably knew it. Like, I always say that the media was in on us from the beginning. They knew in the summer of 2016 what was going on. They knew the Clinton campaign was playing Fusion GPS. It was the House Republicans who had to figure it out. but and make it public it only people who didn't know was donald trumpin and the republicans in this country now but all the major",
