    "turn_idx": 104,
    "turn_text": "Probably let me start with your last question. I mean, the only mistake that I made is trusting our FBI and DOJ knowing now, if I would have known then what I know now, we would have been blasting out subpoenas left and right in March. But, well, actually it would have been in January. So the reason that I figured out that there was something going wrong, that was the leak of the Flynn-Kisley Act conversation. Okay? That is a major leak that it should have sent shivers through DOJ and FBI. They should have had every single available FBI agent in the country. trying to track down who would leak a call between the incoming national security advisor and the Russian ambassador. Nobody ever got to the bottom of that. Nobody did a real investigation of it. So that's why we were looking for the improper surveillance. And what we found was that there were the Trump transition officials were being caught up in intelligence reports and then being unmasked. And some of those actually were leaked to the press, which I can't get into which ones those were. but another more examples of things that should have been prosecuted. So that's what happened in March. And if you remember, just so the story is correct for your listeners, they brought me under the Democrats on the left, started accusing me of leaking information. And so what happened at the time is all I stepped aside from leading the Russian investigation into Russian election interference, but I continued at that point to look into FISA abuse and other matters and unmaskings, which essentially was the real investigation in all this because we already knew at the time in March that there was that there was nothing that there was no collusion between the Trump campaign and Russia.",
